      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "GDPR compliance for your French stationery shop hinges on a few core principles, like having a clear, lawful reason to collect data, which is a principle of data minimization. You must only collect the email and shipping addresses absolutely necessary for fulfilling an order, like sending a shipment or sending a receipt. Remember, you need a solid legal basis, like the contract itself, to process this personal information. If you don't need it, don't keep it, or you'll be in trouble with the regulators.",
